## 📦 Runtime Dependencies

✅ **Use this command:**

```bash
npx expo install [package-name]
```

❌ **Do NOT use:**

```bash
npm install [package-name]
yarn add [package-name]
```

📌 **Reason:**  
Using `npx expo install` ensures the installed package versions are compatible with the current Expo SDK, preventing version mismatches and runtime errors.

---

## 🛠️ Development Dependencies

✅ **Use this command:**

```bash
yarn add [package-name] -D
```

❌ **Do NOT use:**

```bash
npx expo install [package-name]
npm install --save-dev [package-name]
```

📌 **Reason:**  
`expo install` is not intended for development tools. Use `yarn` to add tools like linters, test libraries, etc., as dev dependencies.

---

## 🧠 Summary

| Type         | ✅ Correct Command               | ❌ Wrong Commands                                          |
|--------------|----------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| Runtime      | `npx expo install`              | `npm install`, `yarn add`                                  |
| Development  | `yarn add [package] -D`         | `npx expo install`, `npm install --save-dev`, `yarn add -D` |

